.TITLE "ssh"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Connects to a remote host securely. It uses the __Secure Shell protocol__ to provide an encrypted communication channel for logging into and executing commands on a remote machine.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**ssh user@host**
Connects to a remote machine using the specified username and hostname.
> __user__ remote username | __host__ remote IP or domain

**ssh -i path/to/key user@host**
Connects using a specific private key for authentication.
> __-i__ identity file flag | __path/to/key__ private key path

**ssh -p 2222 user@host**
Connects to a remote host using a non-standard port number.
> __-p__ port flag | __2222__ port number

**ssh -L 8080:localhost:80 user@host**
Sets up local port forwarding to tunnel traffic through the SSH connection.
> __-L__ local forward flag | __8080:localhost:80__ forwarding rule

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Securing your __ssh__ access with public key authentication instead of passwords is a critical security best practice. You can manage your keys using the __ssh-agent__ to avoid entering your passphrase for every connection.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:scp** **mac:ssh-keygen**

